      h2 Migrating from AI SDK Elements# @36,3367,632,21
      text AI Elements replaces , and we are going to deprecate AI SDK Elements. @36,3400,632,20
      link "AI SDK Elements" https://elements.ai-sdk.dev @36,3432,632,21
      text You do not need to migrate right away. The components you installed from AI SDK Elements were copied into your project, so they keep working. @36,3465,632,40
      text When you are ready, each pattern page has a migration prompt. Paste it into your coding agent, and it rebuilds the wrapper in components/ai-elements on Trace, Code Block and the other shadcn/ui components. Every export keeps its name and props, so the code that uses it does not change. @36,3517,632,82
      text See for the element that replaces each file, and for the elements we did not rebuild. If you still need one of those, and we will help you build it. @36,3611,632,40
      link "Migrating from AI SDK Elements" /docs/ai-elements#migrating-from-ai-sdk-elements @36,3663,632,20
      link "open an issue" https://github.com/shadcn-ui/ui/issues/new?template=feature_request.yml @36,3695,632,21
      link "Read the Docs" /docs/ai-elements @36,3728,632,20
      h2 September 2026 - cn @36,3760,632,21
      text Every shadcn component now imports cn from the cn package. @36,3793,632,21
      text For years, every shadcn project started with the same five lines in lib/utils.ts: import clsx, import twMerge, wrap one in the other, export it as cn. It worked, but it meant two dependencies and a helper you had to copy into every project and every registry. @36,3826,632,60
      text We have moved that into a package. is a drop-in replacement for . It is smaller, faster and ships the same API, so nothing changes at the call site. @36,3898,632,41
      row @36,3951,632,20
        link cn https://github.com/shadcn-ui/cn @36,3951,17,20
        text twMerge(clsx(...)) @65,3951,118,20
      card @36,3983,632,99
        button Copy @53,3998,598,37
        text import { cn } from "cn" ;<div className={cn("flex items-center", className)} /> @53,4047,598,20
      h2 What changed# @36,4094,632,21
      text Registry components, blocks and examples import cn from cn instead of @/lib/utils. @36,4127,632,21
      text npx shadcn init installs cn and generates a one-line lib/utils.ts. @36,4160,632,20
      text Every registry item that uses cn declares it as a dependency, so npx shadcn add installs it in projects created before this change. @36,4192,632,40
      h2 lib/utils.ts# @36,4244,632,22
      text The utils registry item still exists. It now re-exports cn so your own code keeps working and you still have a single place for project helpers. @36,4278,632,40
      card @36,4330,632,131
        text lib/utils.ts @53,4345,598,21
        button Copy @53,4378,598,36
        text export { cn } from "cn" @53,4426,598,20
      h2 Existing projects# @36,4473,632,21
      text Nothing breaks. Your lib/utils.ts keeps working and new components install cn next to it. To move the rest of your project over and drop clsx and tailwind-merge, run the migration: @36,4506,632,41
      card @36,4559,632,149
