      h2 Zero configuration# @36,5189,632,21
      text If you are logged in to the GitHub CLI, there is nothing to set up. @36,5222,632,21
      card @36,5255,632,98
        button Copy @53,5270,598,36
        text gh auth login @53,5318,598,20
      text When a repository is not publicly readable, the CLI reads it through gh using your stored credentials. The token stays inside the GitHub CLI. It never enters the shadcn process. @36,5365,632,41
      card @36,5418,632,98
        button Copy @53,5433,598,36
        text ✔ Using gh credentials. ✔ Checking registry. ✔ Created 1 file: - lib/auth.ts @53,5481,598,20
      h2 CI support# @36,5528,632,22
      text Where the GitHub CLI is not installed, set GH_TOKEN or GITHUB_TOKEN: @36,5562,632,20
      card @36,5594,632,99
        button Copy @53,5609,598,36
        text npx shadcn@latest add acme/internal-toolkit/auth-kit @53,5657,598,21
      text We recommend a fine-grained personal access token scoped to the repository with Contents: Read-only access. @36,5705,632,40
      h2 Works with every command# @36,5757,632,21
