      h2 How it works# @36,6466,632,22
      text Public repositories are read anonymously, exactly as before. No credentials are used and the GitHub CLI is never invoked. @36,6500,632,40
      text The CLI tries anonymous access first and only uses your credentials when the repository is not publicly readable. @36,6552,632,41
      text Private files are read through GitHub's Contents API, pinned to the resolved commit SHA. @36,6605,632,20
      text A token from GH_TOKEN is only ever sent to api.github.com. Stored GitHub CLI credentials are read by gh, not by the CLI. @36,6637,632,41
      text See the docs for the full guide. @36,6690,632,20
      link "Private repositories" /docs/registry/github#private-repositories @36,6722,632,20
      h2 August 2026 - Human in the Loop @36,6754,632,22
      text @shadcn/helpers can now mock human-in-the-loop flows for the AI SDK. A scripted conversation can pause for real user input, wait for an approval, and continue with whatever the user decided. @36,6788,632,60
      text Everything streams through the real useChat lifecycle, so your tool cards, approval prompts, and question flows behave exactly as they would in production. @36,6860,632,41
      card @36,6913,632,200
        button Copy @53,6928,598,36
        text import { createChat } from "@shadcn/helpers/ai-sdk" const chat = createChat<ChatMessage>() .user("Help me plan the next prototype.") .assistant(({ writer }) => { writer.text("A couple of questions before I start.") writer.tool("askQuestions", { input: { questions } }) }) .assistant(({ writer, toolCall }) => { writer.text( toolCall?.name === "askQuestions" && toolCall.output ? `Starting with ${toolCall.output.answers.direction}.` : "Starting now." ) }) @53,6976,598,122
      text Pass needsApproval to pause behind the user's decision. The scripted output streams after approval, and denial streams automatically. @36,7125,632,41
      card @36,7178,632,159
        button Copy @53,7193,598,36
        text chat .assistant(({ writer }) => { writer.text("That will archive 3 drafts. I need your approval.") writer.tool("archiveDrafts", { input: { count: 3 }, needsApproval: true, output: { archived: 3 }, }) }) .assistant(({ writer, toolCall }) => { writer.text( toolCall?.approved ? "Archived 3 drafts." : "Okay, leaving them in place." ) }) @53,7241,598,81
      link "Read the Docs" /docs/helpers/ai-sdk#human-in-the-loop @36,7349,632,21
